            <ArticleTitle>Cost and Potential Avoidability of Antibiotic-Associated Adverse Drug Reactions in Children.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/jpids/pix096</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We identified 375 children who visited the emergency department or urgent care clinic at Children's Mercy Hospitals &amp; Clinics for antibiotic adverse drug reactions over a 1-year period, and the total cost for these visits was $170 893.20. Of these ADRs, 17% were likely avoidable. The potential negative consequences of antibiotics should be considered at the point of prescribing.</AbstractText>
